    "project_quote": "An architecture where structural honesty and spatial generosity converge to create a human-centered workplace for a densifying financial district.",
    "project_team": null,
    "project_collaboration": null,
    "project_summary_1": "<strong>A Structural Expression that Liberates the Contemporary Workplace</strong><br>Rising 100 metres above GIFT City’s evolving skyline, Suma Shilp reimagines the contemporary commercial tower through an architecture where structure, workspace, and human experience become inseparable. Located within India’s emerging financial district, the project responds to increasing urban density by balancing commercial performance with spatial flexibility, environmental integration, and a distinctive architectural identity.<br>Rather than adopting the conventional glass-box typology, the tower is conceived as a structural proposition that allows the building itself to become its defining architectural expression.",
    "project_summary_2": "<strong>Structure as Architecture</strong><br>This commercial tower is a masterclass in balancing high-density performance with architectural poise. Set upon a compact rectangular footprint, the design utilizes a centralized core to anchor its vertical circulation and services, liberating the building’s entire perimeter for expansive, column-free workspaces. An 11-metre structural grid creates expansive, column-free floor plates, capable of accommodating diverse organizational requirements while maximizing daylight and panoramic views across the city.",
    "project_summary_3": "The tower’s defining feature is an exposed steel exoskeleton that enables a dramatic cantilevered volume to float above the base. More than a visual statement, this structural system of intricate bracing transfers loads outward and downward, allowing the interior to remain open and highly flexible. Here, the building’s architectural identity emerges directly from its structural logic, where the means of support are deliberately expressed rather than concealed.",
