    "project_services": "Masterplanning, Architecture (DPR), Engineering (DPR),  Landscape Design (DPR)",
    "project_quote": "Architectural Place-Making to Engage People in Immersive, Info-training Experiences",
    "project_team": "<strong>Project Director</strong><br>Jayesh Hariyani<br>Mistri Adi<br><strong>Project Associate Director</strong><br>Harsh Goel<br><strong>Design Lead - Architecture</strong><br>Saumil Mevada<br>Rakhi Rupani <br><strong>Design Lead - Landscape</strong><br>Harsh Goel<br><strong>Project Manager </strong><br>Saumil Mevada<br><strong>MEPF Director</strong><br>Parth Joshi<br><strong>Operations Director</strong><br>Bindu Hariyani<br><strong>Operations Manager</strong><br>Chintan Thanki<br><strong>Project Team</strong><br>Viresha Hariyani <br>Bansari Trivedi <br>Jigar Jobanputra <br>Meet Panchal <br>Manan Patel <br>Dharmesh Panchal <br>Chintan Sitapara <br>Mayur Panchal <br>Ishit Shah <br>Ashad Mehmood <br>Nivedita Patel <br>Jigar Thakkar <br>Drashti Amin <br>Krutarth Nanavati <br>Bhargav Dave <br>K.A. Mohammed Asif <br>Rajvi Shah <br>Mahesh Karande <br>Meet Patel <br>Vivek Joshi <br>Ketan Patel <br>Rushikesh Wadnere <br>Viral Yadav <br>Neha Karode <br>Rucha Agnihotri <br>Shalvi Patel <br>Mohammed Irfan Shaikh <br>Paresh Dholakia <br>Bhargav Bhavsar <br>Dharmesh Gangani <br>Sanjay Mistry <br>Pranav Kumar <br>Jignesh Raval <br>Suhel Makandar <br>Harshad Gadher <br>Vaibhav Trivedi <br>Uday Modi <br>Nilesh Prajapati <br>Meeta Goel <br>Ashish H Shrimali <br>Ankit Arora <br>Mahesh Prajapati <br>Sagar Gandhi <br>Rajesh Patel <br>Amit Mehta <br>Kiran Vaidya <br>Vishnu Prajapati <br>Amish Panchal <br>Vipul Dalwadi <br>Amrut Mundhava <br>Mitesh Mistri <br>Shalin Shah <br>Naresh Jadav <br>Manisha Gaddamvar <br>Ghanshyam Patidar <br>Dhvanit Sharma <br>Nikunj Bhavsar <br>Ankit Patel <br>Parth Sutariya <br>Vinod Parmar<br>Sachin Safi <br>Aswin Patel <br>Bhargav Bhavsar <br>Abhijeet Verma <br>Bhargav Patel <br>Nirav Shah <br>Shyam Tomar <br>Rajvi Jain <br>Keval Vejani <br>B V Shukla <br>Khyati Anjaria <br>Mosmi Mehta",
    "project_collaboration": "Jones Lang Lasalle (JLL)",
    "project_summary_1": "<strong>Celebrating Maritime Heritage:</strong><br>The Government of India and its Ministries of Shipping and of Culture conceived and commissioned the creation of a National Maritime Heritage Complex at Lothal, the town where part of the ancient Indus Valley civilization was excavated and identified by the UN as an international heritage site. Being established as the world’s most ancient man-made dockyard, Lothal was the favored site for this project, which aims to showcase, inform and educate about the long, rich and diverse maritime history of the Indian subcontinent. Attractions within the complex include light-and-sound shows, boat rides, and an experiential theme park.",
    "project_summary_2": "<strong>An Architecture Reflecting Ancient Roots:</strong><br>One of the major constituents of this complex is the National Maritime Museum having displays in 14 exhibit galleries beginning with mythological references and Harappan accounts, passing through Vedic and Mauryan periods, and tracing traditional ship-building techniques to the arrival of Vasco Da Gama and other Europeans. The exhibits include maritime activities under British rule, post-colonial India as well as present day oceanic research. Like the citadel of ancient cities, this museum complex sits as the nucleus of the central lake in Lothal’s upper town area (acropolis).",
    "project_summary_3": "The design vision is inspired by the ancient civilization’s grid like arrangement and rich urban fabric with the museum’s blocks, having inclined outer walls clad in regional stone bricks just like the ancient dockyard and warehouse structures in Lothal. The various sectional blocks are arranged around a central open courtyard where a massive relic ship is installed over a waterbody. The roofs of the blocks pitch upwards to accommodate north-lights to illuminate the exhibits adorning the galleries’ interiors, simultaneously visually referencing a set of ships with sails aloft. As one approaches the ceremonial entrance to the structure, a massive tower with lights projecting from its peak can be seen atop the central block housing the reception lobby, akin to a lighthouse.",
    "project_featured_image": "https://inidesignstudio.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/National-Maritime-Heritage-Complex-Featured-Image.jpg",
    "project_image_1": "https://inidesignstudio.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/National-Maritime-Heritage-Complex-Cover-Images.jpg",
    "project_image_2": "https://inidesignstudio.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/Interior-scaled.jpg",
